 'northrop-pmd-tanks':source('northrop-pmd-tanks','Propellant Management Device Tanks','Northrop Grumman','https://www.northropgrumman.com/what-we-do/space/mission-enabling-products/pmd-tanks','The manufacturer describes its PMD tank family as all-titanium for long-duration propellant compatibility.','The MEL uses this family as a benchmark. Actual vessel selection, alloy, shell gauge, external finish and mounting design remain allocated. Bare titanium should not be rendered as gold foil unless a separate blanket is assigned.','Product-family description above PMD tank tables','manufacturer product description'),
 'northrop-pressurant-tanks':source('northrop-pressurant-tanks','Pressurant Tanks','Northrop Grumman','https://www.northropgrumman.com/what-we-do/space/mission-enabling-products/pressurant-tanks','The supplier offers both monolithic titanium and composite-overwrapped pressure vessels for gases including helium.','The family name alone cannot decide the installed bottle construction. Selecting either titanium or carbon overwrap is a project allocation until a matched vessel is identified.','Product-family description','manufacturer product description'),
 'jpl-juno-vault':source('jpl-juno-vault','Juno Jupiter Orbit Insertion Press Kit — Electronics Vault','NASA / JPL-Caltech','https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/juno/spacecraft/','Juno uses a titanium electronics vault for its Jovian radiation environment.','Titanium in the workbench is an explicitly inferred shielding material. Juno does not establish the LEO design’s thickness, dose attenuation, secondary-particle response or mass allocation.','Spacecraft chapter: Electronics Vault','mission agency description'),
 'nasa-copv':source('nasa-copv','Deceptively Complex: Composite Overwrapped Pressure Vessels','NASA Engineering and Safety Center','https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/nesc/deceptively-complex-composite-overwrapped-pressure-vessels-copv-remain-a-challenge-for-engineers-to-unravel/','NASA describes a pressure-retaining liner surrounded by a composite overwrap and discusses carbon-composite implementations.','A wound-fiber depiction is appropriate only for an explicitly allocated COPV. It does not establish the liner material, fiber/resin system, winding schedule, pressure rating or life.','COPV construction and carbon-composite discussion','NASA engineering assessment overview'),
 'ariane-s400':source('ariane-s400','400 N Bipropellant Apogee Motors — S400-12 / S400-15','ArianeGroup Orbital Propulsion Centre','https://www.space-propulsion.com/spacecraft-propulsion/apogee-motors/','The supplier specifies a platinum-alloy chamber and throat for the S400 family, with film and radiative cooling.','The table does not identify the entire expansion-bell alloy. A neutral metallic bell is a visual allocation with unresolved material, not evidence for niobium, carbon, steel or an all-platinum nozzle. The Aerozine study is not an S400 flight configuration.','Characteristics table: Chamber/Throat Material and Cooling Control','manufacturer product data'),
 'nasa-ammonia-materials':source('nasa-ammonia-materials','PD-ED-1209 — Ammonia-Charged Aluminum Heat Pipes with Extruded Wicks','NASA Goddard','https://extapps.ksc.nasa.gov/Reliability/Documents/Preferred_Practices/1209.pdf','Goddard documents aluminum/ammonia heat-pipe practice and a metal/fluid compatibility table including aluminum and stainless steel with ammonia.','This is a compatibility precedent, not qualification of the workbench pumped loop or heat-lift concept. Its near-room-temperature heat-pipe practice does not establish high-temperature refrigerant or seal suitability.','Pages 1, 5 and 6–7; Table 2','NASA preferred reliability practice'),
 'glenair-spacewire':source('glenair-spacewire','963-080-26 SpaceWire-Type Cable','Glenair','https://cdn.glenair.com/speedline/pdf/963-080-26.pdf','This cable combines copper-alloy conductors, FEP insulation/jacket, aluminum-polyimide pair shielding and a silver-plated copper outer shield.','Polyimide can be a buried shield layer; it is not necessarily the visible jacket. The workbench harness construction and exterior wrap are allocations, not a replica of this specific cable.','Cable Construction table','manufacturer data sheet'),
 'glenair-space-interconnect':source('glenair-space-interconnect','Low-Profile Micro-D Connector Specifications','Glenair','https://www.glenair.com/micro-d/low-profile-metal-and-plastic-shell-micro-d/pdf/connector-specification.pdf','The supplier specifies copper-alloy contacts with gold over nickel, with different materials for the connector shell, insulator and mounting hardware.','Gold is assigned only to small connector/contact details as a study finish. This does not select a flight connector or justify gold coloring for structural frames, pressure vessels or whole optical terminals.','Materials and Finishes table; revision 12/20/18','manufacturer data sheet'),
 'dunmore-beta-cloth':source('dunmore-beta-cloth','Beta Cloth','Dunmore Aerospace','https://www.dunmore.com/products/beta-cloth.html','The supplier describes Beta cloth as PTFE-impregnated glass cloth used in spacecraft protection layers.','A white woven protective cover is a material allocation, not evidence of a complete MMOD shield. Impact performance depends on the complete tested stack and its spacing.','Beta Cloth product description','manufacturer material description'),
 'sheldahl-redbook':source('sheldahl-redbook','The Red Book — Revision E','Sheldahl','https://www.sheldahl.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/RedBook.pdf','The handbook distinguishes aluminized polymer films, glass-cloth covers and protective coatings, including separate exposed-metal and exposed-polymer optical behavior.','Film orientation, substrate, thickness and added coatings matter. A blanket color or a texture cannot choose solar absorptance, thermal emittance, charging behavior or atomic-oxygen durability.','January 24, 2020 Revision E; Thermal Control Overview; MLI Blanket Materials','manufacturer material handbook'),
 'nasa-pcb-materials':source('nasa-pcb-materials','Workmanship — Printed Circuit Board Product Assurance','NASA Office of Safety and Mission Assurance','https://sma.nasa.gov/sma-disciplines/workmanship','NASA describes multiple PCB dielectric families and identifies glass-reinforced polyimide as a commonly used laminate for NASA applications.','The COTS accelerator board laminate, copper stackup, solder mask and radiation capability are not established by this reference. Visible board details remain generic study representations.','PCB product assurance: laminate dielectric materials','agency engineering guidance'),
 'edmund-optical-glass':source('edmund-optical-glass','Fused-Silica Optical Windows and Broadband AR Coatings','Edmund Optics','https://www.edmundoptics.com/p/25mm-dia-3mm-thick-nir-i-coated-lambda4-fused-silica-window/45477/','The supplier describes fused-silica windows with wavelength-specific antireflection coatings for optical systems.','This is a material/appearance precedent only. It does not identify the flight-terminal prescription, aperture window, spectral coating, glass grade or radiation performance. A subtle colored reflection is an illustrative coating response.','Product Details; Technical Information','optical manufacturer reference'),
 'anywaves-sband-radome':source('anywaves-sband-radome','Product Portfolio — S-Band TT&C Antenna','Anywaves','https://content.anywaves.com/hubfs/Anywaves-Datasheets/PORTFOLIO-ANYWAVES_compressed.pdf','The S-band TT&C data sheet specifies a Vespel protective radome with SG121FD white paint on flight models.','This is evidence for the cited benchmark antenna only. The workbench’s generic patch still has an unselected radome/paint system. Other Anywaves antenna products use different radome materials; a shared ivory texture does not identify polymer chemistry.','Printed page 7 / PDF page 7: Protective Radome row; compact variant on page 9 is separate','manufacturer data sheet')
